    {
      "finding": "No concrete scoped source blocker. All non-navigation HTTP bytes are exactly retained; the five full byte-splice operations restore the complete C0/current HTTP source.",
      "scope": "All five complete production files, all four complete test files, narrow existing HTTP delta"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Closed four-field account/network/run decoding and exact UTF-8 comparison reject malformed/foreign tuples. Dedicated expected-account/run mutation routes reject legacy fallback. Successful mutations require matching account/run/contract acknowledgment headers; malformed success remains uncertain.",
      "scope": "Captured native authority"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Prepared intents capture workspace, lease generation and native run. Synchronous actor consumption precedes suspension; at most one dispatch per UUID in this store lifetime. Native acknowledgment is remembered and synchronously delivered to the required owner callback before any awaited readback. Failed later lease/readback returns a known ACK with nil private snapshot; outer AnyApplicationSession may separately cancel delivery.",
      "scope": "Dispatch and owner retirement"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The bounded256 in-memory attempted-ID set is deliberately not a durable or cross-store journal. Consumers must retain one current store/owner; a recreated store or process restart needs a separately qualified durable reconciliation contract. No automatic retry or older unbound POST exists in these methods.",
      "scope": "Conservative no-replay limits"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Original Workspace/Home/Archive/Widget kinds518/32/48/112 are read from saved admitted catalog mappings and signed evidence. Present empty and unsupported source values do not manufacture defaults. Current Home is separate and retains absent, explicit empty, builtin and exact opaque object choices; reads require current membership and destination existence.",
      "scope": "Original versus current Home"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The exact captured last-opened descriptor is checked with canonical typed bytes, preserving typo/null/false/arrays. No archived timestamp is replayed. Live local datetime definition, bounded whole-second time, single exact target, nonempty version, empty shared changeId and no rejection are required before known ACK.",
      "scope": "Actual-open local metadata"
    },
    {
      "finding": "This commit supplies Engine/Host contracts only. N24 server lifetime/run fencing and bound-route acceptance, real completed-migration cold context, UI/gestures, physical Apple and crash-recovery acceptance remain separate. Its synthetic loopback test fixtures do not prove those outcomes.",
      "scope": "Backend and UI activation"
    }
